 "path": ".openclaw/tmp/continual_arc-notes.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC reusable observation\n\nObserved task family: a distinctive small multicolor-grid object is copied to every translated placement whose corresponding cells in the noisy background are all the background's sparse color (0), while preserving original object and all other cells. Demonstration: a 7-cell object in color 1 on color-3/0 noise yielded copies at positions where each of its seven shape cells mapped to 0; the test analogous color-5 object on color-9/0 noise yielded two copies. Practical method: record the object's exact occupied-cell offsets from its bounding-box top-left, scan every in-bounds translation and require all those positions to be 0, then recolor just those matching cells with the object's color. Preserve everything else. This is a pattern-level heuristic evidenced by one task, not a guaranteed global rule.\n"
}
